# Cloudflare Pages headers (documents/heart-audio-engine.md, section 11).
#
# Every path is cross-origin isolated, which is what gives the page
# SharedArrayBuffer and Heart its fastest mode; tools/serve.mjs sends the
# same three headers on localhost.
#
# Code, HTML, worklets and heart.wasm change in place with every push, so
# they are revalidated on every load and a push is live for returning
# visitors at once. Only the recordings under /audio are cached for a year,
# so a recording must never change in place: a new take gets a new name.
# The manifests beside them do change, and are revalidated like code.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# A header set by two matching rules is joined with a comma, so the rule
# above's Cache-Control is detached here before the long one is set.
/audio/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# the sample manifests and loop lists, which are edited in place
/audio/*.json
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
